WEBVTT

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.870
Singularity of unknown origin has
appeared at coordinates 125°-979.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:19.980
It is beginning to expand.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.090
Gravitational anomaly detected.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.250
Internal mass increasing at a geometric rate.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.500
Evasive maneuvers! Now!

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.000
Propulsion problem on Proto-Valiancer Unit 2.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.730
He won't last much longer at his current velocity.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.300
What's wrong, Unit 2?!

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.180
Accelerate!

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:34.680
Damn...

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.720
Damn it!

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.900
Spread your wings

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.530
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.820
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:03.200
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.460
That world you see before your eyes

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:18.050
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.520
The pain of loss isn't something

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.480
You want to get used to, and yet

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:30.440
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.400
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.240
Can't go back

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.660
Want to go home

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.990
The two of them back-to-back

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.040
Break through

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.790
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.130
Like painting over a colorless world

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.840
Let this sympathy reach

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.100
Let's build the future that we envision

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.310
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:11.110
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.740
Wake up, Watase Aoba!

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.850
Okay, okay.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.440
On to the next topic:

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.650
With regards to "Nectoribium,"

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.750
an ore that was discovered in the Couchard Mine in northwest Zogilia,

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.190
Honestly! You're gonna be late right at the start of a new school term.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:51.950
the Zogilia state government has stated

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.530
I'll be fine as long as I take the train that leaves in 12 minutes.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.060
that they believe there is a high chance that it is a revolutionary natural resource

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.490
Geez... Are you sure?

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.410
with the potential to replace all sources of energy.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.900
Thanks for the breakfast.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.200
And that they intend to begin

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:01.320
full-scale mining and development operations in the near future.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.100
High school kids sure have it rough commuting.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.450
Quiet, middle-schooler.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.270
Tsubasa, hurry up and get ready.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.460
Okay.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.960
Well, I'm off then.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.410
See you later!

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.840
Take care!

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.770
I might've cut it a little close.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.680
I made it somehow.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.440
Aoba!

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:40.740
Over here.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.720
Hey, long time no see!

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.370
What did you do over the summer break?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.080
I went to Hawaii.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:45.740
Really?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.290
Good morning.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:00.880
No, I'm telling you it's for real.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:01.690
Good morning!

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:01.970
For real?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:02.760
Morning!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.840
Yo.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.550
Our seat changes are up.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.270
Whoa, I'm in the front row.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.520
I'm in the back.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.940
Lucky!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.520
Let's see...

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.040
Aoba, you're next to Yumihara.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.030
Oh.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.370
Good morning, Yumihara.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.370
G-Good morning, A-A-Aoba-kun.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.330
Nice to meet you.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.600
Nice to meet you too...

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.010
Since this is your first day of the second term,

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.970
be sure to go over your schedule.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.470
And your first midterms are in October.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.140
Yumihara Hina.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.580
She's a returnee from abroad

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.480
who came back to Japan in April and enrolled at this high school.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.190
That's all I know.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.780
She's been acting kind of cold,
like stiff and formal, towards me.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.620
Did I do something to upset her?

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.290
Got it.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.330
What?

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.040
Here.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.550
Are you okay?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.390
I-I-I'm fine!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.430
Thank you.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.430
Uh, sure...

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.890
By the way, why have you been so stiff and—

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.890
Watase! Yumihara!

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.600
What are you doing?

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.900
Oh, no... We're not really...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.270
It's nothing.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.110
I'm really sorry about that.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.950
Oh, dammit!

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.790
So, Aoba wins again?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.500
He's a merciless jerk.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.590
All right! Then it's my turn next.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.220
Sure.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.390
Aoba, did you do something to that returnee from abroad?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.300
Huh? You mean Yumihara?

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.370
Yup. It's Hina-chan, isn't it?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.060
She's cute, huh?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.810
I'm jealous, Aoba.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.080
Huh? You're not making any sense.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.900
I haven't done anything.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.280
But you know, ever since the entrance ceremony,

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.570
it's like she's been watching you and only you.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.160
I was talking. That's not fair.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.080
There's no rule that says I have to wait.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.360
He's good at basketball, don't you think?

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.770
In middle school, we were on the same basketball team.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.810
But I ended up getting injured.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.570
I picked this school

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.970
because it's close to the hospital where I get physical therapy.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.310
And then Aoba got it in his head to come here, too.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.370
Look over there!

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.370
It's not like it's his fault I got injured.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.280
It made me happy.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:25.590
Because I was nervous about going to another high school all by myself,

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.960
on top of being injured.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.510
Isn't he a great guy?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.470
What?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.680
Hey, Yumihara.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.020
What's it about Aoba that you like?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.520
It's not like I...

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.920
What just happened?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.220
Where am I?

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:13.800
What are my coordinates?

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.560
Is the clock out of whack?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.260
It's the year 2014?!

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.140
It can't be...

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.150
I've traveled through time?

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.320
In other words, this is the past?

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:36.110
If that's true...

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.290
I'm definitely in the past.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.070
What's up with this kind of security?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.340
That's right!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.500
That's definitely you,

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.760
Watase Aoba!

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.760
To think that I'd run into you here of all places!

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:00.970
I'm coming for you.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:13.860
What's this?

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.250
What's wrong?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.130
I got a disaster advisory.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:17.920
Feel the shake?

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.330
Nope. Maybe it's a false alarm?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.660
Yeah, maybe.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.290
A-Aoba-kun...

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.120
Everyone!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.570
Hm? What is it?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:28.400
Hey, look at that!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:37.840
What the hell is that thing?

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.720
So you <i>did</i> come.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.000
What's that thing?

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.060
It's huge.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.730
What a stupid look you've got on your face, Watase Aoba!

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.990
It's a look that says you never even
dreamed that I'd show up here!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:01.450
However, this is no dream!

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:10.790
Run!

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.640
Damn it!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.810
What the hell is going on?!

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.970
This way!

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.570
Ryutarou! Junichi!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.370
So it's after <i>me</i>?!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.870
Why can't I hit him?!

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.500
The targeting information isn't precise enough?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.430
Do I need to manually aim it?

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.510
Damn! I'm out of ammo?!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.430
Why's that thing after Aoba?!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.350
Junichi, I'm borrowing this!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.680
Borrowing what?!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.310
This is the end!

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.320
What the hell...?!

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.290
If it's me you're after, follow me!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.290
Don't fuck around with me!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.540
Hey, there's something flying this way!

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.850
That's a robot, isn't it?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.810
Everyone, run!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.770
What's with everybody?!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.900
Scurrying around in such tight quarters...

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.570
You think you can escape from me?

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.200
Where'd it go?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.870
Yumihara?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.330
Follow me!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.080
Why?!

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:16.210
Why would you—

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.000
There's no time!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:17.990
Hurry!

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.010
H-Hey!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:34.600
Damn it!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.150
CVP-014A, boot-up!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.870
Where'd she go?!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.750
It's over!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.130
What the hell?!

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.980
Another one?!

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.430
Boot-up process: all green.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.850
I made it in time!

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.810
That's...

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:23.130
Wait!

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:26.820
Get in!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:27.850
Yumihara?

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.150
Hurry up!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:39.080
It can't be...

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.320
Are you really the Yumihara I know?

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.300
Be quiet.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.720
Why?

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.390
Why in hell?!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:53.680
Why?!

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.520
Hina, why?!

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.450
Tell me why, Hina!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.700
I know. I just need this one time.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.050
Goodbye.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:41.980
Amazing!

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.120
Rounds of ammo left: 2

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.080
The enemy's energy reading has been terminated.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.620
You defeated him?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.450
Yes.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.000
Wh-Wh-What are you looking at?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.670
Are you okay?

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:04.090
I'm fine!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:05.970
Can I ask you about something?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.300
About what?

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.170
Everything.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.890
All right.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.070
I think you'll find it hard to believe,

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:22.730
but I came to this world from the same future as the person who was piloting that robot.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:24.900
You mean...

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.840
We're time travelers.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.860
I am...

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:30.900
And so was he.

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:35.200
Then what about this thing?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.620
This robot, too?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:37.540
That's right.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.700
It came from the same future.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:43.120
But it's getting rickety in all sorts of places now.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:50.520
I've been watching over you the whole time I've been here.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.930
Over me?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:52.720
Yes.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.220
Over Watase Aoba.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:54.640
All this time...

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.640
The Aoba from the past which I hadn't met yet. That's you.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:04.400
Today, when we ended up seated next to each other,

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.310
I was really surprised.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.250
I'd never imagined, even in my wildest dreams,

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.070
Good morning!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:09.690
Morning!
that there'd come a time when
we'd be sitting next to each other.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.320
Yo.
that there'd come a time when
we'd be sitting next to each other.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.740
Our seat changes are up.
that there'd come a time when
we'd be sitting next to each other.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:13.360
Our seat changes are up.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.370
You seem mystified.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:23.540
But I couldn't afford to be apart from you.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.880
Because I knew that one day he would come to kill you.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.010
Why?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.410
That's because...

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:35.510
You told me he would.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.010
Whoa, hey.

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:45.560
Things are about to get crazy here!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.270
Aoba, get off.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:48.060
Wh-What?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.280
My job here is done.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.740
I was able to defeat the enemy who wanted you dead.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.700
You should return to your ordinary life again.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.280
You can forget about this story of people from the future.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:01.370
Hold on Yumihara, what are you going to do?

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.620
Run, of course.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.370
I don't want to get caught, after all.

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.040
You're going back... to the future?

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.170
I don't know any way to do that.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.500
I'm just going to run, that's all.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.220
Just run? But where are you going to go?

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.840
With a giant robot like this, once you've been spotted...

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.200
I know that!

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.720
But right now I don't have any other choice, do I?!

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.390
I <i>know</i>!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.080
Hina, even after that beating,

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.910
even in death, there's still something I can do!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.010
Don't tell me he plans to self-destruct?!

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:47.620
What?

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.210
Eject!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.040
It won't open!

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.060
Hey, we're taking damage!

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.090
It's falling apart due to lack of maintenance!

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.480
I never imagined that you were over here, Hina.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.320
I knew that you'd be coming.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.030
I see.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.280
In that case, do you know what happens after this, too?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.160
You're going to die, along with Watase Aoba and me!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.130
This is...

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.550
The singularity...

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.420
I see.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.340
So that's it.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:40.800
Hang on tight.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.640
Hina, what are you planning to do?!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.770
What are you thinking?

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.420
I finally understand.

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.230
So, this is how it was fated to be.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.400
Fated?

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.400
I've always wondered...

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.570
Why you appeared before me...

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.250
Why I have been unable to forget you...

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:04.450
Yumihara?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.700
It's Hina.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.660
Hina?

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.120
Aoba, you have to trust me.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.590
All right, Hina.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.550
You trust people too readily!

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:21.380
You plan to leap in there?!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.850
It's starting to close!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.740
Here we go!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.390
Aoba.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:07.930
This is goodbye.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.140
Huh?

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.390
Goodbye?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.690
You're going to the future now.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.740
To the future?

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:16.650
What about you?

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.490
Dio is waiting.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.520
Huh?

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:22.320
Who?

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:30.950
Wait!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.500
What's going on?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:33.570
Hina?!

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:34.750
What is this?!

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:36.960
What in the world is this?!

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.580
Dio is waiting, Aoba.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.080
Hina...

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:57.000
Dio...

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:58.820
Dio, do you read?!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:00.530
This is Dio.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.440
I have two on my tail.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.570
Things are getting hairy!

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.610
Sorry, I've got my hands full here, too!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.360
Sorry, me too, Dio!

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:08.160
I'll handle it somehow!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.370
Dio?

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.310
Concentrate your firepower!

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.140
Company, get them under effective fire, stat!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.640
Targets are moving too fast!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.390
Retreat! All vehicles, retreat!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.150
First Anti-Aircraft Artillery Battalion
is no longer combat-worthy!

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:39.360
This is bad!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.440
We probably don't have much ground force left, do we?

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.480
We have to fight them without cover fire, then?!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.370
What <i>is</i> all this?!

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:54.410
The Luxon's Feeling Match number is rising!

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:56.120
What are you saying, Corporal Nasu?!

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:59.250
Wait, Mayuka, there's no one aboard that one, right?

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.460
But the reading...

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:04.210
And the matching with Dio is incredible!

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:06.470
Who the hell is matching with me?!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:08.640
Where the heck am I?!

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:09.430
Where's Hina?!

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.390
Nice Coupling.

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:20.880
With my heart, I call out

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:25.260
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:29.770
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:34.400
Just for now, please

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:38.570
I know you

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:43.070
I'm searching for you

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:45.530
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:52.170
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:52.170 --> 00:23:00.720
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:05.300
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:09.850
and the times I have wondered

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:14.100
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:16.360
I want to save you,

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:18.440
I want to protect you

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:22.820
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:25.700
Wait for me

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:30.450
The love we'll surely find

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:35.250
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:42.020
Next episode, on Buddy Complex: "Nice Coupling."
